    "body": "I think I missed the worker case. When a script URL for a worker is a local URL, it doesn't get to http fetch. So, currently that worker client won't get a controller. (i.e. it's just null.) We have related text here - https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#selection - but I think we should add relevant steps to \"set up a worker environment settings object\". It should inherit either worker's document's controller or worker's worker's controller in this case I suppose.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
